  "title": "BER: Fix undefined behavior in OCTET STRINGs",
  "description": "Check if the calculated end offset overflows.\n\nAlso prevent undefined behavior by not left-shifting a signed\ninteger. Per X.680 8.2, \"The [tag] number is a non-negative\ninteger,\" so really get_ber_identifier should have a pointer to\nan unsigned integer for the tag number. (Although in practice,\ntag numbers that large only exist when some kind of error has\noccurred.)\n\nOSS-Fuzz Issue 453516726",
